WEBVTT

00:00:03.609 --> 00:00:09.560
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Monday the thirtieth. Um, can everyone hear me, or am I talking to myself again?</v>

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:15.029
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, we've got you. Bit of an echo, but it's all right.</v>

00:00:17.109 --> 00:00:23.410
<v David Whitfield>Better than the broken coffee machine in the canteen. That's not making any noise at all. Grim start.</v>

00:00:25.809 --> 00:00:31.059
<v Sarah Okafor>You were cheerful enough at the charity bake sale on Friday. Three brownies, wasn't it?</v>

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:34.939
<v David Whitfield>Two. The other one was structural support for the plate.</v>

00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:40.520
<v Marcus Hale>There's a birthday cake in the office as well, apparently. We're basically running on sponge.</v>

00:00:41.899 --> 00:00:46.450
<v Hannah Price>Please tell me it's not another one with someone's face printed on it.</v>

00:00:47.590 --> 00:00:51.789
<v Priya Raman>Sorry, just getting my headset on. Caught the important bit about cake.</v>

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:58.750
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, actual factory stuff. I tested the guard switch on two yesterday and it's all fine now. That's closed.</v>

00:00:59.439 --> 00:01:02.240
<v David Whitfield>That was the one that wasn't making properly?</v>

00:01:04.590 --> 00:01:08.790
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, that one. Tested and fine, not another job for this morning.</v>

00:01:09.730 --> 00:01:15.329
<v Callum Reid>And I already swapped the filter on the number two bearing yesterday. That's done as well.</v>

00:01:17.579 --> 00:01:22.480
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah so, I finished the repair on the fire panel last night. Repair's complete.</v>

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:27.900
<v Priya Raman>Right, the panel repair, rather than the monthly test?</v>

00:01:29.829 --> 00:01:33.329
<v Aisha Begum>Exactly. Two separate things. The repair's out of the way.</v>

00:01:35.489 --> 00:01:41.790
<v Callum Reid>One observation from nights: noticed the GT1 fuel valve was running a bit warm, but it settled down.</v>

00:01:42.219 --> 00:01:45.719
<v Marcus Hale>Ah, okay. Settled back down, then, not still sitting warm?</v>

00:01:46.489 --> 00:01:51.040
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, settled. Just passing on what happened, not raising another job off it.</v>

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:58.090
<v Hannah Price>Mine's still the same blocker. Can't get to the big boiler until production gives us a window.</v>

00:01:58.450 --> 00:02:03.000
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. That's still blocked, then, not something we're agreeing to get into today.</v>

00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:06.150
<v Hannah Price>Exactly. Nothing changed there.</v>

00:02:08.430 --> 00:02:14.030
<v Marcus Hale>And the supplier still hasn't confirmed the delivery for the Stretch Wrapper. Still stuck on that.</v>

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:17.500
<v Callum Reid>Not even a definite delivery confirmation?</v>

00:02:18.969 --> 00:02:22.120
<v Marcus Hale>Nope. Same position as before. Just reporting the blocker.</v>

00:02:24.009 --> 00:02:26.810
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. I'll send the shift handover report round.</v>

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:32.569
<v Callum Reid>Cheers, Sarah. Easier than trying to piece it together from the chat.</v>

00:02:34.949 --> 00:02:43.699
<v Sarah Okafor>There's also the training records for the new starters that need sorting. That's a whenever you get a chance one. Anyone able to take it?</v>

00:02:44.449 --> 00:02:48.300
<v Callum Reid>Um... I can't put my name against that at the minute.</v>

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:52.750
<v Hannah Price>No, I can't commit to those either.</v>

00:02:54.889 --> 00:02:59.789
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, nobody on the training records, then. Still needs doing, but no owner agreed.</v>

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:05.060
<v David Whitfield>Yeah, don't want a vague nod turning into someone's name on it.</v>

00:03:06.849 --> 00:03:11.400
<v Priya Raman>I'll run the monthly fire alarm test. It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:15.900
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks. Priya Raman on the monthly fire alarm test, then.</v>

00:03:16.610 --> 00:03:17.810
<v Priya Raman>Yep, that's mine.</v>

00:03:18.439 --> 00:03:24.039
<v Aisha Begum>And just so the two don't get muddled, that doesn't reopen the repair. That bit's finished.</v>

00:03:24.639 --> 00:03:27.789
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, understood. Routine monthly test, separate from your repair.</v>

00:03:29.129 --> 00:03:36.479
<v Sarah Okafor>Han, can you inspect the Boiler Feedwater Pump for leaks tomorrow at 9:30? Not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:43.909
<v Hannah Price>Sorry, no, I can't take that one tomorrow at 9:30. That time doesn't work for me.</v>

00:03:44.289 --> 00:03:53.740
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, Priya, can you take that instead? Inspect the Boiler Feedwater Pump for leaks tomorrow at 9:30. Same thing: not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:03:55.689 --> 00:04:00.939
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, I'll take it. I'll inspect the Boiler Feedwater Pump for leaks tomorrow at 9:30.</v>

00:04:02.819 --> 00:04:07.020
<v Marcus Hale>That's an inspection for leaks we're talking about, yeah? Not a strip-down?</v>

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:12.210
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, inspection for leaks. That's what I'm taking on.</v>

00:04:13.750 --> 00:04:17.600
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. Doesn't need emergency treatment, but that time needs to hold.</v>

00:04:17.930 --> 00:04:20.029
<v Hannah Price>Thanks, Priya. Sorry for bouncing it.</v>

00:04:21.329 --> 00:04:26.579
<v Sarah Okafor>Han, can you replace the seals on the Boiler Safety Relief Valve at half two?</v>

00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:29.379
<v Hannah Price>Half two today, yeah?</v>

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:33.149
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, at half two.</v>

00:04:35.290 --> 00:04:41.589
<v Hannah Price>Okay, I can do that. I'll replace the seals on the Boiler Safety Relief Valve at half two.</v>

00:04:42.569 --> 00:04:46.069
<v David Whitfield>Sorry, you clipped there—seals on the valve, not the pump?</v>

00:04:47.509 --> 00:04:50.660
<v Hannah Price>The Boiler Safety Relief Valve, yeah. That's my one.</v>

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:56.920
<v Callum Reid>Right, I had those times the wrong way round for a second.</v>

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:06.069
<v Sarah Okafor>It's Priya on the Boiler Feedwater Pump tomorrow at 9:30, and Han on the Boiler Safety Relief Valve at half two.</v>

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:10.069
<v Priya Raman>Yep, pump tomorrow at 9:30. Got it.</v>

00:05:10.449 --> 00:05:13.250
<v Hannah Price>And valve seals at half two. We're straight.</v>

00:05:15.269 --> 00:05:22.269
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. And the training records are still unclaimed. The whenever you get a chance bit isn't an assignment to anyone.</v>

00:05:23.870 --> 00:05:26.319
<v Callum Reid>Yep. Nobody's picked those up in here.</v>

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:33.259
<v Marcus Hale>Well, that was almost as complicated as dividing the office cake into equal slices.</v>

00:05:34.329 --> 00:05:36.430
<v David Whitfield>Without coffee, basic arithmetic's beyond me.</v>

00:05:36.819 --> 00:05:38.019
<v Aisha Begum>We did notice.</v>

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:43.259
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before this becomes a performance review of the canteen, that's us.</v>

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:45.310
<v Priya Raman>Cheers, everyone.</v>

00:05:45.649 --> 00:05:46.850
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks all. Bye.</v>
